BT /F3 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 294.4 Tm (No work starts on your property until DHS&EM or the independent Debris Monitor confirms your packet is complete and the property is authorized.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 282.8 Tm (A site assessment comes first. Hazardous materials \(chemicals, fuels, propane, batteries including lithium, possible asbestos or lead\) are removed) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 271.2 Tm (separately. Then remaining eligible fire debris \227 collapsed burned materials, household debris, appliances, scrap metal, and authorized vehicles \227 is) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 259.6 Tm (hauled away. Standing walls, roofs, and foundations are not removed under this work. Cleanup is limited to living, recreational, and working areas of) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 248 Tm (the authorized property unless the State directs otherwise in writing. Metal, burnt vehicles, and appliances go to recyclers when practicable; other) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 236.4 Tm (non-hazardous debris generally goes to the Tok landfill.) Tj T* ET
